.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt JUGGLER 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm juggler
.Nd architecture and JSON-RPC wire format for the llama-server control plane
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the control plane for local
.Xr llama-server 1
instances managed by the clown ecosystem.
It owns a registry of running llama-server children in memory and
exposes an RPC surface to its clients.
.Pp
This page documents the control-plane architecture and the JSON-RPC
wire format.
The daemon is invoked as
.Cm juggler daemon .
The job platform it once shared a binary with was extracted into the
standalone
.Ql code.linenisgreat.com/ringmaster
module.
For the daemon's CLI surface and the client that drives it from a terminal
see
.Xr juggler 1 .
.Sh ARCHITECTURE
The system is three processes:
.Bl -tag -width "juggler"
.It Cm juggler daemon Pq Xr juggler 1
The daemon.
Listens on a Unix domain socket
.Pq see Sx CONTROL SOCKET ,
maintains a single-host in-memory registry of llama-server children,
and reaps them on exit.
Run by
.Xr launchd 8
or
.Xr systemd.user 5
under the
.Sq programs.juggler
home-manager module.
.It Xr juggler 1
The CLI client (same binary as the daemon, different subcommand).
Thin wrapper around the JSON-RPC client SDK.
Every subcommand
.Pq Cm start , stop , status , list , models
issues exactly one RPC and pretty-prints the result.
.Pq Cm download No is the exception \(em it still uses the in-process bubbletea progress UI against jugglermodels.Download directly, not the RPC.
.It Xr llama-server 1
The actual inference engine.
Started by
.Nm
as a child process, identified by its
.Fl -alias .
Binds 127.0.0.1:<random-port> by default and serves the OpenAI-/Anthropic-
compatible HTTP API.
.El
.Pp
Clients
.Pq Xr juggler 1 , Xr clown 1
talk only to
.Nm ;
they never start
.Xr llama-server 1
directly.
This loose-proxy split means clients see exactly one persistent
endpoint
.Pq Nm Ap s socket
while the underlying inference servers can come and go.
.Sh CONTROL SOCKET
.Nm
binds the path resolved from:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
The
.Fl -socket
flag on
.Cm juggler daemon
when present.
.It
The
.Ev JUGGLER_SOCKET
environment variable when set.
.It
.Pa $HOME/.local/state/juggler/control.sock
as the default.
.El
.Pp
Clients use
.Xr os.Stat 3
on the socket path before dialing, so a missing socket produces a
deterministic error path that points at the home-manager module rather
than a confusing
.Sq connect: invalid argument
on macOS
.Pq the kernel rejects nonexistent UNIX socket paths longer than 104 bytes with EINVAL, not ENOENT .
.Sh WIRE FORMAT
The control socket speaks newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"ListInstances","params":{}}\(rsn
.Ed
.Pp
Each line is one envelope.
Response envelopes carry the same
.Sq id
as their request so a client serializing multiple in-flight requests
on the same connection can match them up.
The Go client SDK in
.Pa internal/juggler
mints sequential numeric IDs.
.Pp
Methods:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "MethodListAvailableModels" -compact
.It Sy MethodStartInstance
.It Sy MethodStopInstance
.It Sy MethodStopAll
.It Sy MethodListInstances
.It Sy MethodGetInstance
.It Sy MethodListAvailableModels
.It Sy MethodDownloadModel
.It Sy MethodListModels
.It Sy MethodAddRemoteModel
.It Sy MethodRemoveRemoteModel
.It Sy MethodResolveModel
.El
.Pp
See
.Xr juggler 1
for the per-method semantics.
.Sh MODEL REGISTRY
.Nm
tracks two kinds of model:
.Sy local
.Pq a GGUF file spawned as a Xr llama-server 1 child, the pre-existing kind
and
.Sy remote
.Pq a registered, process-less gateway endpoint, e.g. OpenRouter .
.Cm ListModels
returns the union of both, each entry tagged with its
.Sq Kind .
.Pp
The remote registry is a small TOML file at
.Pa ~/.local/share/juggler/models.toml ,
overridable via
.Ev JUGGLER_MODELS_PATH .
.Cm AddRemoteModel
and
.Cm RemoveRemoteModel
upsert and delete entries in that file by name; see
.Xr juggler 1
for the
.Cm model
CLI that drives them.
.Pp
Each
.Ql [[model]]
entry has these keys:
.Bl -tag -width "token_file" -offset indent -compact
.It Sy name
the registry name.
.It Sy style
.Ql anthropic ,
.Ql openai-compat
or
.Ql decisions
.Pq the last is consumed only by Cm juggler decide ; No it is not a loop codec and Cm prompt No rejects it .
.It Sy url
the endpoint base URL.
.It Sy token
a literal secret or a
.Ql ${VAR}
reference.
.It Sy token_file
a path
.Po
.Ql ~/
and
.Ql $VAR
expanded
.Pc
to a file whose trimmed contents are the token: the by-reference credential
for a host with no secret in its models file.
When set it takes precedence over
.Sy token ;
setting both is a configuration error.
.It Sy model
the upstream model id sent to the provider; the registry
.Sy name
is then a stable alias for it.
Empty means the name itself.
.El
.Pp
.Cm ResolveModel
turns a bare model name into a runnable endpoint, checking in order:
.Bl -enum -compact -offset indent
.It
the remote registry
.Po
an exact name match returns its registered
.Sy style No unchanged, its
.Sy url ,
its
.Sy token
.Pq read from Sy token_file No when set
and its upstream
.Sy model ,
with any
.Ql ${VAR}
references expanded against the resolving process's environment
.Pc \&;
.It
an already-running local instance of that name
.Pq reused, not restarted ;
.It
a local GGUF file under
.Pa ~/.local/share/juggler/models ,
started fresh via the same path as
.Cm StartInstance .
.El
.Pp
If none match,
.Cm ResolveModel
returns
.Sy -32001 .
.Pp
The first step needs no daemon.
.Cm juggler run ,
.Cm juggler decide
and
.Cm juggler spawn
resolve a remote entry directly from the models file
.Pq Ev JUGGLER_MODELS_PATH ,
with the same expansion and
.Sy token_file
handling, so a system-service user needs only a models file and a
credential reference in its own state directory.
A name with no remote entry sends them to the daemon, which remains
required for local llama-server instances because it owns the process.
.Sh AGENT SUBSTRATE
FDR 0019
.Pq Pa docs/features/0019-juggler-agent-substrate.md
makes juggler the substrate for short, headless, tool-using agents with no
worktree and no terminal, each under its own principal.
This page documents only the shape; the verbs are in
.Xr juggler 1 .
.Bl -tag -width "evaluator" -offset indent
.It The loop
.Cm juggler run
reads a brief
.Pq the contract the spawner signs: principal, parent, room, model, system, task, inline moxyfile, REQUIRED tool allowlist, evaluator, limits
and drives the model's tool-use protocol through one moxy upstream
until the model ends its turn, calls the mandatory
.Ql cannot_complete
tool, hits the step cap or the wall clock, or \(em with
.Ql evaluator.stop_on_pass
\(em the evaluator first passes.
A run that ends inside a reply
.Pq cannot_complete , a tool transport failure, an evaluator pass
leaves that reply's remaining tool calls requested and unanswered: not
executed, no tool_result, no ledger entry.
Two codecs project the loop's stanza-shaped turns onto a provider's wire:
OpenAI-compatible chat completions and Anthropic Messages.
.It The ledger
One entry per tool call
.Pq name, declared artifact kind, ok, URIs, error
plus how the loop ended
.Pq Ql end_turn , cannot_complete , step_cap , timeout , tool_error , model_error , max_tokens , evaluator_pass .
A call's URIs come from the MCP result's
.Ql structuredContent
first, then from its content blocks.
A call whose declared kind is read-only
.Pq Ql list , search , read , get , query
records no URIs, so read-only tools must declare such a kind; every
other call keeps all its URIs, a
.Ql madder://
blob link
.Pq moxy's store for an oversized result, which may hold the product
included.
Success is measured, never reported: the model never claims it.
.It Pa traffic.jsonl
.Pq clown#255
The ledger carries no call arguments; circus's attestation and coverage
agent graphs need them after the run, but the evaluator's input and the
signed contract must not grow with file bodies.
.Cm juggler run
instead writes one line per tool call to
.Pa traffic.jsonl ,
keyed by BOTH the agent's principal and its ringmaster job
.Pq Pa traffic/<principal>/<job>.jsonl under the store root ,
at the same point its ledger entry is appended \(em including a
read-only kind, an invalid-arguments call and a tool transport error.
Keying by job, not principal alone, matters because a bare
.Cm run Fl -brief
with no
.Fl -job
starts a FRESH job every invocation under the SAME principal: keying by
principal alone would let a second run of the same brief silently
overwrite the first run's file underneath an already-printed path.
The path is also outside
.Pa agents/<principal>/ ,
which is moxy's own working directory: folio-style tools auto-allow
writes inside CWD, so a traffic file living there would be reachable \(em
readable, deletable, replaceable \(em by the very model turn whose calls
it exists to audit.
Each line:
.Sy {"step":N,"job":"...","tool":"...","args":{...},"args_digest":"...","result_size":N,"ok":bool,"ts":"..."} ,
arguments in full, the result's size in bytes and ok flag only
.Pq never the result body: moxy already blobs an oversized one, and the ledger carries its URI .
.Ql job
makes a line self-identifying even copied out of its directory; the
loop itself (jugglerloop) has no notion of a job, so it leaves the
field empty and the writer that owns the path stamps it before each
write.
Each ledger call entry gains
.Ql args_digest :
a sha256, hex-encoded, over the arguments' canonical JSON encoding
.Pq object keys sorted, no insignificant whitespace, numbers kept as their original text; see Fn jugglerloop.CanonicalJSON No and Fn jugglerloop.ArgsDigest ,
so a ledger entry and its traffic line are joinable without the ledger
itself carrying the arguments.
Written within a run, truncated on the next run of the SAME job
.Pq an adopted Fl -job No retry; a fresh job gets its own file, never the prior one's ,
never read by the evaluator.
Durability is NOT the ledger's: each line is flushed as its call
completes, while the ledger is written once, at the very end of the
run \(em so a run killed mid-flight can leave traffic lines on disk with
no ledger at all, the opposite of a half-written ledger with no
traffic.
Opening or writing the file can fail
.Pq a crowded disk, a permissions problem .
An operator-supplied principal or job id that is not a safe single
path segment
.Pq e.g. a Fl -job No value containing a slash, or starting with a dot
disables traffic before ever trying to open it, for the same reason.
Every case is best-effort, never fatal to the run, but leaves a note
in the ledger's
.Ql notes
array \(em naming the actual cause, not a generic failure \(em so an
auditor does not mistake silence there for a complete record.
.Cm juggler clean
.Pq clown#250
reaps a resolved run's traffic files once past its age guard;
.Pa agents/<principal>/
itself still has no sweep.
A model API token or key is never among a tool's recorded arguments: it
rides the model request, a wire this file never touches.
Whatever secret a model's tool call DOES carry \(em a token pasted into
a query, a password typed into a form-filling call \(em lands verbatim
here, unfiltered: this file is as sensitive as the tool arguments
themselves.
Both
.Cm juggler run Ap s
and
.Cm spawn Fl -wait Ap s
stdout grow a
.Ql traffic
path field beside the existing
.Ql ledger
one.
.It The evaluator
A jq program, run embedded over the ledger JSON, that must produce exactly one
boolean
.Pq an error, no output or a second output is false .
Only an
.Ql end_turn
or
.Ql evaluator_pass
with a true final verdict is
.Ql succeeded .
A brief that sets
.Ql evaluator.stop_on_pass = true
.Pq off by default
ends the run with
.Ql evaluator_pass
as soon as the evaluator, run over the in-progress ledger after a
successful tool result, first returns true.
That per-call check has its own 2-second evaluator budget, not the run's
wall clock, so a pass that coincides with the deadline can end the run
up to about 2 seconds late; a holder's cancel is unaffected.
.It The lifecycle
Each agent is one systemd transient unit started by
.Cm juggler spawn ,
its principal minted under a per-run root.
Before minting anything,
.Cm juggler spawn
checks systemd's own readiness to start units
.Pq Ql systemctl is-system-running ;
.Fl -user
checks
.Ql systemctl Fl -user
instead:
only
.Ql running
and
.Ql degraded
proceed, anything else refuses the spawn synchronously with the
manager's state
.Pq Ql unknown , No with a Ql detail No explanation, when systemctl's own exit carried no state at all ,
recorded for a subagent spawn in the run ledger as
.Sy {"tool":"systemd","kind":"refusal","ok":false,"reason":"...","state":"<state>","detail":"..."} .
.Cm juggler run
is a ringmaster producer
.Pq start at boot, progress per turn, done at the end ;
it holds the job's advisory lock
.Pq Fn jobwake.AcquireJobLock
for the whole run, acquired right after the job exists and released only
after done has returned
.Pq clown#256 .
The unit's post-stop hook is the first-line backstop that runs for
every unit.
Ringmaster's host-wide liveness reaper
.Pq Em ringmaster#33
is the backstop FOR the hook: any long-running
.Cm ringmaster monitor
or the standalone
.Cm ringmaster reap
scans every channel on the host, not only the one it is itself a
consumer on, so a juggler job needs no monitor of its own on its own
channel
.Pq Cm juggler spawn launches none .
A job whose lock is released without a terminal record
.Pq the hook also never ran: systemd itself gone
is reaped by the host-wide reaper
.Pq any Cm ringmaster monitor No or Cm ringmaster reap No on the host ,
one grace period after the first reaper observes the released lock,
including after a reboot.
A host running neither still has the gap the hook exists to cover;
deploying one is the host's own responsibility
.Pq e.g. a Ic ringmaster reap No systemd unit the host deploys .
A lock already held by a live producer
.Pq Va jobwake.ErrAlreadyLocked
refuses the run outright rather than racing it; any other acquire failure
is not fatal but is recorded in the run's ledger
.Ql notes ,
not only stderr.
The unit's
.Ql ExecStopPost
hook
.Cm juggler exit-wake
is the sole exit-wake emitter, writing the terminal record when the main
process left none and waking every holder of the job once.
A losing race against the reaper
.Pq or any other writer
on either one's own done call is ringmaster's exit 3
.Pq Va jobwake.ErrAlreadyTerminal ;
both relay whichever terminal actually landed and report success, never a
failure.
.Cm juggler
exact-matches the installed
.Cm ringmaster Ns 's
.Ql version Fl -protocol
against the protocol it was built for, lazily and once per process,
refusing loudly on any mismatch before the first real job-platform call;
on an adopted job
.Pq Fl -job Ar id , which skips Ic start
the check runs explicitly before the lock is taken; a mismatch there exits
1 and writes nothing.
.Cm juggler exit-wake ,
the terminal writer of last resort, skips the check and only warns on a
mismatch: it must never refuse to settle a job over a protocol drift
already caught loudly at spawn or run time.
.El
.Pp
Ringmaster's four terminal states map onto FDR 0032 D6's exit reasons:
.Bl -column "interrupted" "normal" "when" -offset indent
.It Sy state Ta Sy reason Ta Sy when
.It succeeded Ta normal Ta loop ended cleanly and the evaluator was true
.It failed Ta failed Ta evaluator false, cannot_complete, step cap, wall clock, unrecovered tool error
.It aborted Ta shutdown Ta a holder cancelled the job
.It interrupted Ta crash Ta the unit died without a verdict
.It interrupted Ta killed Ta the unit's main process died on a signal
.El
.Pp
The router,
.Cm juggler decide ,
is not an agent: one Decisions-API request whose outcome is a
.Ql route
entry in the run ledger, kept by the lifecycle owner.
The run ends with
.Cm juggler resolve ,
which stops whatever is still running, closes the ledger with the
fallback's own outcome and wakes the issuer.
.Sh JSON-RPC ERROR CODES
Codes follow JSON-RPC 2.0 §5.1.
.Nm
uses:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -offset indent
.It Sy -32601 Pa Method not found
The requested
.Sq method
is not implemented by the server.
.It Sy -32602 Pa Invalid params
The
.Sq params
payload could not be unmarshalled into the expected shape.
.It Sy -32603 Pa Internal error
Reserved for marshal failures on the server side.
.It Sy -32000 No through Sy -32099 Pa Server-defined application errors
.Nm
uses
.Sy -32000
for general application errors
.Pq launcher not configured, download failure, etc.
and
.Sy -32001
for a
.Sq not found
condition, reused across methods with a method-specific message:
.Cm GetInstance
alias-not-found,
.Cm RemoveRemoteModel
unknown remote-model name, and
.Cm ResolveModel
no local or remote match.
.El
.Sh INSTANCE LIFECYCLE
On
.Cm StartInstance :
.Bl -enum -compact -offset indent
.It
Pick a free TCP port via
.Fn net.Listen :0
+ close.
.It
Resolve the
.Sq model
parameter to an absolute GGUF path
.Pq Pa $modelsDir/<name>.gguf No when not absolute .
.It
.Xr exec 3
.Xr llama-server 1
with
.Fl -port ,
.Fl -host ,
.Fl -alias ,
.Fl -model
plus any pass-through args.
SysProcAttr.Setpgid=true so the daemon can signal the entire
process group on Stop.
.It
Insert
.Pq under l.mu
the
.Sy child
record into
.Sq l.children Ns Bq alias .
.It
Call
.Fn reg.Add ;
on failure, roll back the children entry, SIGKILL the child, drain
its
.Sq exited
channel, return the error.
.It
Poll
.Pa /health
every 250 ms for up to 60 s.
On failure, SIGKILL + drain + error.
.It
Launch the single Wait-owner goroutine that calls
.Xr exec.Cmd.Wait 3 ,
populates
.Sq ch.waitErr ,
and closes
.Sq ch.exited .
.It
Launch the reaper goroutine which blocks on
.Sq ch.exited
and, under l.mu, removes the alias from both
.Sq l.children
and the registry if and only if
.Sq l.children Ns Bq alias == ch
.Pq the identity guard ensures Stop is the single owner of the cleanup when both fire concurrently .
.El
.Pp
On
.Cm StopInstance :
.Bl -enum -compact -offset indent
.It
Under l.mu, look up and delete the
.Sq l.children
entry.
.It
.Xr kill 2
.Sy -pid Pq the process group No with Sy SIGTERM .
.It
Wait on
.Sq ch.exited
or 5 s of grace, whichever first.
.It
On timeout, SIGKILL and wait again
.Pq the Wait owner goroutine is guaranteed to close ch.exited eventually .
.It
.Fn reg.Remove
the alias.
.El
